#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161704 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "59ea7ebb-5b69-5551-a5b9-c286e2730881" :question/math-academy-id "e-8160" :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ Evaluate the function when $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= ax \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-5) + 0 \\cdot 8 + 4 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-15 + 0 + 20 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161705 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "30204c69-3362-5cc1-a04a-3bb83559b300" :question/math-academy-id "e-8161" :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$, given by\n\n$B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1$\n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$\\qquad$ $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2} \\\\ y_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{2} - x_{2}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{3} - x_{3}y_{1} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 4 - 2 + 3 - 2 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "34398117-07f4-51d9-a879-30a0f6891e68" :question/math-academy-id "e-8162" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Write down a bilinear form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{y}$ in terms of the components of $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + (-1)x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} + (-2)x_{2}y_{2} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2y_{1} - y_{2} \\\\ 3y_{1} - 2y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= x_{1}(2y_{1} - y_{2}) + x_{2}(3y_{1} - 2y_{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161707 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "84e1b597-45d7-51f4-aaa9-8a52c753a510" :question/math-academy-id "e-8163" :question/problem "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 2x_{2}y_{1} - x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 0x_{1}y_{2} + 0x_{1}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 2x_{2}y_{1} + 0x_{2}y_{2} + 0x_{2}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 0x_{3}y_{1} + (-1)x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$, $b=2$, and $c=-1$. Finally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a81cae-2e28-5951-ba79-203ce68a2de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160879} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b2fc95-c847-5875-8bd8-75e17ef55ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160880} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a0e28d-4f6c-5279-87f8-9d357bdecbdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160881} {:answer/id #uuid "23dc65e4-c125-5a43-8f2d-4b4d68f73f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160882} {:answer/id #uuid "6179d155-9120-5995-9d4a-73799db9674a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b2fc95-c847-5875-8bd8-75e17ef55ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160880} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6214574-4200-561c-a3a8-32986bbb557b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160878}] :question/id #uuid "2cfb9520-59d9-5ad8-a887-b4fdde98c9f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94040" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}a & -2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x, y) = x_{1}y_{1} - 2x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a + b$?"}]}
